              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Clean Air Act (CAA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 42 U.S.C. §7401
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1970, 1977, 1990
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Authorizes the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) to establish National Ambient
                  | Air Quality Standards (NAAQS) to protect public health and welfare from hazardous
                  | air pollutants. The law regulates air emissions from stationary and mobile sources.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Occupational Safety and Health Act (OSHA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 29 U.S.C. §651
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1970
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Ensures worker and workplace health and safety by providing a place of employment
                  | free from recognized hazards such as exposure to toxic chemicals, excessive noise
                  | levels, mechanical dangers, heat or cold stress, or unsanitary conditions.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Clean Water Act (CWA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 33 U.S.C. §1251
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1972
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Establishes the fundamental structure for regulating discharges of pollutants into
                  | U.S. waters and quality standards for surface waters (e.g., pollution-control programs
                  | such as setting wastewater standards for industry and permit programs to control discharges).
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Safe Drinking Water Act (SDWA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 44 U.S.C. §300
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1974, 1986, 1996
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Protects the quality of water that may be designated for drinking use, whether from
                  | surface water or ground water sources. EPA establishes minimum standards to protect
                  | tap water and requires all owners or operators of public water systems to comply with
                  | health-related standards.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Toxic Substances Control Act (TSCA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 15 U.S.C. §2601
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1976, 2016
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Provides EPA authority to require reporting, record-keeping and testing requirements,
                  | and restrictions relating to chemical substances or mixtures during production, importation,
                  | use, and disposal of chemicals. Chemicals include polychlorinated biphenyls (PCBs),
                  | asbestos, radon, and lead-based paint. Other substances, such as food, drugs, cosmetics,
                  | and pesticides, are generally excluded.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Federal Insecticide, Rodenticide, and Fungicide Act (FIFRA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 7 U.S.C. §136
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1947, 1972, 1996
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Governs the registration, distribution, sale, and use of pesticides in the United
                  | States. All pesticides distributed or sold in the United States must be registered
                  | (and licensed) by EPA. According to the statute, a pesticide is any substance or mixture
                  | of substances intended for preventing, destroying, repelling, or mitigating any pest
                  | or for use as a plant regulator, defoliant, or desiccant, or any nitrogen stabilizer.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 42 U.S.C. §4321
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1969
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Ensures that all branches of government give proper consideration to the environment
                  | prior to commencing any major federal action that significantly affects the environment.
                  | The most notable NEPA requirements are Environmental Assessments and Environmental
                  | Impact Statements, which are assessments of the likelihood of impacts from alternative
                  | courses of action. Projects governed by this statue include airports, buildings, military
                  | complexes, highways, and parkland purchases.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 42 U.S.C. §6901
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1979, 1986
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Gives EPA the authority to control hazardous waste from “cradle to grave,” including
                  | generation, transportation, treatment, storage, and disposal. RCRA also sets a framework
                  | for management of nonhazardous solid wastes by focusing on waste minimization and
                  | phasing out land disposal of hazardous waste.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xblx-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation, and Liability Act (CERCLA, or
                  | Superfund)
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 42 U.S.C. §9601
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') 1980, 1986
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Provides a federal “Superfund” to clean up uncontrolled or abandoned hazardous-waste
                  | sites in addition to accidents, spills, and other emergency releases of pollutants
                  | and contaminants into the environment. EPA is authorized to implement the Act in all
                  | 50 states and the District of Columbia and all U.S. territories. The identification,
                  | monitoring, and response activities in Superfund sites are coordinated through the
                  | state environmental protection or waste management agencies.
