        p.a-subtitle Table 13
        p.m-data-table__caption
          | Overview of Vaccine Recommendations for Pregnant Women in the United States.
          a(href='#t13fn1', data-behavior='ShowPopupTip') *
        .m-data-table__table-container
          table.m-data-table__table(role='grid')
            colgroup(span='1')
              col#t13col1(width='17.40%', span='1')
              col#t13col2(width='7.49%', span='1')
              col#t13col3(width='21.53%', span='1')
              col#t13col4(width='53.58%', span='1')
            thead.m-data-table__thead
              tr.m-data-table__row.m-data-table__head1
                th.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__txlx-borders(align='left', valign='bottom', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Vaccine and Type
                th.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__txxx-borders(align='center', valign='bottom', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Category
                th.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__txxx-borders(align='center', valign='bottom', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommendation for Pregnant Women
                th.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__txxr-borders(align='center', valign='bottom', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Comments and Details
            tbody.m-data-table__tbody
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Anthrax, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | May be used in women with high risk of exposure; not recommended for those with low
                  | risk of exposure
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Generally, inactivated vaccines are considered safe during pregnancy, although limited
                  | data from women vaccinated in the U.S. military are of potential concern. The Department
                  | of Defense exempts pregnant women from anthrax immunization, but some women inadvertently
                  | receive the vaccine. In a study of approximately 115,000 live births to military women,
                  | the odds of birth defects were 20% higher for newborns of women vaccinated during
                  | pregnancy than for newborns of women who had never been vaccinated. If exposed to
                  | anthrax, pregnant women should receive the vaccine and 60 days of antimicrobial therapy.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') BCG, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Contraindicated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Although adverse effects have not been associated with BCG vaccination in pregnant
                  | women, it is not recommended during pregnancy, primarily because of theoretical risks
                  | associated with live vaccines. Further studies are needed to prove safety before BCG
                  | vaccine is used in pregnant women.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') HAV, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommended for specific indications
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Recommended for pregnant women who have a history of injection or noninjection illicit
                  | drug use, are working with HAV-infected primates, are working with HAV in a research
                  | laboratory, have chronic liver disease, receive clotting factor concentrates, or are
                  | traveling to or working in countries with high or intermediate endemicity of hepatitis
                  | A.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') HBV, recombinant
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommended in some circumstances
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | A randomized, controlled trial showed seroconversion rates of 92 to 94% among pregnant
                  | women. Older age, obesity, and tobacco smoking have been associated with diminished
                  | HBV vaccine responses in pregnancy. Data on vaccine safety during pregnancy, although
                  | limited, do not suggest any concerns. Pregnant women who have had an HBsAg-positive
                  | sex partner, have had more than one sex partner during the previous 6 mo, have been
                  | evaluated or treated for an STD, or are recent or current injection-drug users should
                  | receive the HBV vaccine. The recommended schedule is 0, 1, and 6 mo, but an accelerated
                  | schedule is possible during pregnancy.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') HPV, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Not recommended
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | If a woman is found to be pregnant during the administration of an HPV series, the
                  | remaining doses should be delayed until after pregnancy is completed. Although there
                  | are limited data for HPV vaccination in pregnancy, the data from vaccine trials and
                  | passive surveillance sources such as pregnancy registries and the CDC- and FDA-maintained
                  | VAERS have not shown any unexpected patterns in maternal or newborn outcomes of HPV
                  | vaccination during pregnancy.
                  sup
                    a(href='#r17') 17
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Influenza virus
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging12.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommended
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | The inactivated vaccine is recommended for all women who are or will be pregnant during
                  | influenza season.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging12(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Live, attenuated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Contraindicated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Because of theoretical risks of fetal infection associated with live vaccines, the
                  | live, attenuated vaccine is contraindicated during pregnancy. However, no worrisome
                  | patterns regarding adverse birth outcomes have been reported in VAERS.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Japanese encephalitis virus, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Inadequate data for specific recommendation
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | There are reports of adverse fetal outcomes after wild-type Japanese encephalitis.
                  | However, given the rarity of infection even in areas where the disease is endemic
                  | and the relatively high risk of adverse events associated with vaccination during
                  | pregnancy, caution should be exercised when considering the use of Japanese encephalitis
                  | vaccination in pregnant women. Vaccination should usually be deferred because of the
                  | theoretical risk to the fetus. However, a pregnant woman traveling to an area where
                  | there is a high risk of exposure to Japanese encephalitis should be vaccinated, assuming
                  | the benefits outweigh the risks.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Meningococcal, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Serotype ACWY conjugate vaccine may be used in the case of a specific indication;
                  | the decision to administer the serotype B vaccine should be based on a risk–benefit
                  | assessment for the patient
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | In the only randomized, controlled trial of maternal meningococcal vaccination, pregnant
                  | women in Mali were randomly assigned to receive either serotype ACWY conjugate vaccine
                  | or influenza virus vaccine. Although the efficacy or immunogenicity results for the
                  | ACWY conjugate vaccine have not been published yet, there were no safety signals in
                  | this trial.
                  sup
                    a(href='#r18') 18
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') MMR, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Contraindicated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Because of theoretical risks associated with live, attenuated vaccine, pregnant women
                  | or those planning to become pregnant should not receive the MMR vaccine. If the vaccine
                  | is inadvertently given to a pregnant woman, she should be informed of the theoretical
                  | risks to the fetus. However, receipt of the vaccine is not an indication for termination
                  | of pregnancy.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Pneumococcal conjugate (PCV13), inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Inadequate data for specific recommendation
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | No published data or recommendations concerning this vaccine seem to exist. However,
                  | given the importance of preventing pneumococcal disease in infants too young to be
                  | vaccinated, a phase 3 trial of PCV13 is being conducted among Gambian women.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Poliovirus, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') May be used if needed
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | This vaccine should not be routinely administered during pregnancy, primarily because
                  | of theoretical concerns, since there has been no demonstrated public health reason
                  | for maternal immunization. However, if a woman is at increased risk for exposure (e.g.,
                  | because of travel to an area where the disease is endemic or possible exposure in
                  | a clinical or laboratory setting), she may be vaccinated after consultation with her
                  | health care provider. No adverse vaccine effects have been observed in pregnant women
                  | or their fetuses.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Pneumococcal polysaccharide (PPSV23), inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Inadequate data for specific recommendation
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Although there are insufficient data for a specific recommendation for pregnant women,
                  | PPSV23 has been used in the second and third trimesters with no evidence of increased
                  | risk. A Cochrane review of randomized, controlled trials determined that there was
                  | insufficient evidence that maternal pneumococcal vaccination reduces the risk of infant
                  | pneumococcal infection.
                  sup
                    a(href='#r19') 19
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Rabies virus, inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') May be used in cases of exposure or a high risk of exposure
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Given that there are severe clinical consequences of inadequately managed rabies infection,
                  | the benefits of administering postexposure rabies vaccine in pregnancy outweigh the
                  | risks. A few studies have shown no increase in the risk of preterm birth, fetal abnormalities,
                  | or spontaneous abortion. If the risk of rabies exposure is high, preexposure vaccination
                  | can be considered. Inadvertent exposure to rabies vaccine during pregnancy should
                  | not be considered a reason to terminate the pregnancy.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Smallpox, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommended after exposure; contraindicated before exposure
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Smallpox is the only human disease that has been eradicated. However, there are concerns
                  | regarding intentional reintroduction (e.g., through bioterrorism) and accidental exposure
                  | (e.g., in a laboratory). Transfer of the vaccine virus to the fetus is rare but can
                  | have severe clinical consequences, including fetal or neonatal death. Therefore, preexposure
                  | vaccination is contraindicated for women who are pregnant or are trying to become
                  | pregnant. However, postexposure vaccination is recommended because the risk of smallpox
                  | to the pregnant women and her fetus outweighs any risk associated with the vaccine.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Tetanus toxoid, inactivated, reduced diphtheria toxoid, and acellular pertussis
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Recommended
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | To ensure passive antibody transfer to the infant, the preferred time of vaccination
                  | is between 27 and 36 weeks of gestation, although vaccination during any stage of
                  | pregnancy is recommended. If a woman does not receive the vaccine during pregnancy,
                  | she should receive it immediately after giving birth. Tetanus toxoid has been shown
                  | to be safe and very effective in pregnant women. Moreover, neonates are protected
                  | against tetanus through antibodies transferred from vaccinated women.
                  a(href='#t13fn2', data-behavior='ShowPopupTip') †
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Typhoid, live and inactivated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Inadequate data for specific recommendation
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Live vaccines such as Ty21a are contraindicated for pregnant women. In situations
                  | with a clear clinical need, inactivated Vi polysaccharide vaccine should be administered.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Varicella, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Contraindicated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Varicella vaccine is contraindicated in pregnancy because of the associated risk of
                  | varicella–zoster virus transmission to the fetus or newborn. However, the effect of
                  | the vaccine virus on fetal outcomes is unknown. Given that the wild-type virus does
                  | not substantially affect the fetus and that the vaccine virus is attenuated, the risk
                  | to the fetus in case of transfer of the vaccine virus is likely to be low. In most
                  | situations, inadvertent vaccination is not a reason to terminate the pregnancy.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxlx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Yellow fever, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Travel and other
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxx-borders(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') May be used if benefit outweighs risk
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xxxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | Yellow fever vaccination is not contraindicated in pregnancy; however, the risks should
                  | be carefully considered. If a pregnant woman cannot avoid travel to an area of high
                  | risk for yellow fever, the decision about vaccination should be made by considering
                  | the risk of yellow fever as compared with the risks associated with the vaccine. If
                  | the vaccination risk is judged to be higher than the disease risk, then the woman
                  | should receive a medical waiver so that she can be in compliance with travel regulations
                  | that require proof of vaccination or exemption on medical grounds.
              tr.m-data-table__row
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xblx-borders.m-data-table__hanging02.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Zoster, live
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Routine
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxx-borders.m-data-table__td--shading(align='center', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1') Contraindicated
                td.m-data-table__entry.m-data-table__xbxr-borders.m-data-table__hanging01.m-data-table__td--shading(align='left', valign='top', rowspan='1', colspan='1')
                  | The target age group for the zoster vaccine (>60 yr) is outside the childbearing years;
                  | pregnant women are unlikely to need this vaccine. Because it is a live vaccine, there
                  | is little public health or clinical justification for administering the zoster vaccine
                  | to pregnant women.
